# Development wildcard DNS for product routes (NFR-4.1 / ISSUE-07).
#
# A browser resolves any name under `.localhost` to loopback by itself, so this service is not needed
# for Chrome, Edge or Firefox. Everything that asks the operating system — Node, `curl`, Playwright's
# API context, a CI container — gets NXDOMAIN, because no platform resolver implements RFC 6761 for
# subdomains of `localhost`. This answers `<anything>.<zone>` with loopback so those clients work too.
#
# The zone is `SEAMNEX_INGRESS_DOMAIN` (`{...}` is CoreDNS's own environment substitution, in a text
# file; compose renders `${...}` before the file is read). Keep the two spellings distinct: they are
# handled by different programs at different times.
#
# `forward` points at the container's `/etc/resolv.conf`, which Docker fills with its embedded resolver
# and that forwards to the host's adapters. This is only safe because the host adapters are *not*
# rewritten: `pnpm dev:dns --apply` adds a Windows NRPT rule scoped to this one zone, so the operating
# system sends only `<zone>` names here. Pointing the adapter itself at 127.0.0.1 would make every
# other lookup travel back into this block and loop.
.:53 {
    template IN A {$SEAMNEX_DNS_ZONE} {
        answer "{{ .Name }} 60 IN A 127.0.0.1"
    }
    template IN AAAA {$SEAMNEX_DNS_ZONE} {
        answer "{{ .Name }} 60 IN AAAA ::1"
    }
    forward . /etc/resolv.conf
    errors
}
